expected_issues.description:
AdapterPoweredChanged only refreshes when `powered` becomes true. If the adapter is powered off, the chooser may keep showing stale Bluetooth-backed ports until another refresh happens. Consider refreshing on both transitions (or explicitly clearing Bluetooth ports on power-off) to keep UI consistent.

```suggestion
void SerialChooserController::AdapterPoweredChanged(BluetoothAdapter* adapter,
                                                    bool powered) {
  // Refresh on any power state change to keep the chooser list in sync.
  GetDevices();
}
```

